Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a structured error frame with the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Streaming Error",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Error status code",
      "minimum": 100,
      "maximum": 599
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Error message"
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Additional details about the resume attempt",
      "properties": {
        "checkpoint_cursor": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Cursor pointing to the last checkpoint in the stream"
        },
        "resume_token": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Resume token that can be used to resume the stream from the last checkpoint"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed as a cyclic redundancy check (CRC) of the serialized key-value pair in the resume token. The CRC algorithm used is the 32-bit CRC with a reflect-in-bit polynomial (CRC-32/IEEE). The CRC value is appended to the serialized key-value pair in the resume token before it is encoded using base64.
